  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A new undoable command, `FaceToSize` (`crates/app/src/commands/face_to_size.rs`), faces a block to height from numbers.\n- The command holds two steps in one `BatchCommand`:\n  - an optional `SetStock`: a box of the stated size, with its top at the top Z;\n  - a normal `CreateOperation`: a Face on `SrcRef::Stock`, from the top Z down to the final Z.\n- The Face uses `top_z` (first stage), `cut_z` (final Z) and `stepdown` (depth per pass). It also uses the stated stepover, cut direction, feed and plunge feed.\n- One undo removes the Face and the stock that the step set. A step that keeps the existing stock does not remove it.\n- The Z values are program Z. The command adds the world Z of the active setup's placed WCS (0 when no WCS is placed). It stores the heights as `Fixed` world Z.\n- The command refuses these inputs by name, at construction. A refusal changes nothing.\n  - a final Z at or above the top Z;\n  - a depth per pass, stepover, feed or plunge feed that is not more than 0;\n  - a stock size that is not three numbers more than 0;\n  - an empty or unknown tool;\n  - a stepover wider than the tool (ribs stay between the rows);\n  - no stock and no stock size;\n  - a top Z below the stock top (the first pass would cut deeper than the depth per pass);\n  - a final Z at or below the stock bottom (the face would cut through the block).\n- A new MCP tool, `face_to_size` (`crates/app/src/mcp/face_to_size_tools.rs`), runs the same command through the session history.\n- A new \"Face to size\" group is at the end of the Stock page (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/stock_face_to_size.rs`). Its button queues `CommandKind::FaceToSize`. The drain runs the same command and selects the new Face.\n- `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` is generated again. The MCP guide names the new tool.\n- The decision record is `docs/decisions/3196-face-to-size.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe issue asks for one step that makes stock and a Face from plain numbers. Before this change, a user had to set the stock, the heights and the operation on three panels.\n\n## Tests\n\nPinning tests:\n- `mcp::face_to_size::face_to_size_on_an_empty_project_makes_stock_and_a_face_and_posts_the_stated_depths`: an empty project, one call. The test generates, verifies and posts with Fanuc. The posted cutting Z levels are `-0.5, -1.0, -1.5`. One undo after the generate removes the Face and the stock. Redo brings both back.\n- `mcp::face_to_size::face_to_size_keeps_the_existing_stock_when_no_size_is_given`\n- `mcp::face_to_size::face_to_size_refuses_bad_numbers_by_name_and_changes_nothing`: each refusal names its number, and no operation or stock enters the document.\n- UI (`camcraft-ui` lib): `the_stock_page_adds_a_face_to_size_as_one_undo_step`, `face_to_size_with_a_ticked_box_sets_the_stock_in_the_same_undo_step`, `a_refused_face_to_size_names_the_number_and_adds_nothing`.\n\nRed before the fix: yes. On unchanged code, the MCP pins fail with `unknown tool 'face_to_size'`.\n\nMutation checks (one guard set to `if false`, then the MCP pins run, then the guard is restored):\n- stepover wider than the tool: red;\n- top Z below the stock top: red;\n- final Z at or below the stock bottom: red;\n- final Z at or above the top Z, with the depth-per-pass guard: red. The plain Face door accepts a level window, so this guard is new behaviour.\n- The restored code is green.\n\nGates on the feature head `f74df8a5d` (before the refresh merge):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 374 of 375 steps ran and passed, 0 failed. The step `ui build (--no-run)` stalled two times: an `sccache` compile of the `hyper_rustls` dependency hung for 60 minutes. That is an environment problem, not a code failure.\n- The UI steps ran directly with cargo and without `sccache` (`env -u RUSTC_WRAPPER cargo test -p camcraft-ui --no-fail-fast`, CWD `crates/ui`): every binary passed, lib 1809 passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 of 6 steps passed.\n- The example catalog suite (`app suites: example_catalog`) is in the quick plan: green. This change does not change a recorded program.\n\nRefresh: upstream main moved 29 commits. I merged it into the branch (head `c03d43451`). The MCP guide row conflicted. I kept upstream's row and added `face_to_size`, and generated `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` again. Checks on `c03d43451`, without `sccache`:\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp --test mcp_doc_drift`: 84 passed and 9 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib`: 1819 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The full quick gate did not run again on the merged head.\n\nAn earlier quick gate run had one red step: `egui_app::tests::dxf_profile::the_stock_page_adds_lists_places_and_deletes_a_dxf_profile`. The new group pushed the DXF profile rows out of the test window. The group now sits under the DXF profiles group. That test is green again.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `*.nc`, `*.cl` or `examples/catalog/**` file changes. The quick plan ran the example catalog suite, and it is green.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full heavy lanes. This is a `P6` PR. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" gives a `P2` or lower PR no heavy step. The light lane ran.\n- Screenshots of the new Stock page group. This headless run has no display. The UI tests assert the labels, the button and the command.\n- A setup with a WCS that is not at the world origin. The code adds the WCS Z, but no test pins it.\n- A camcraft-mcp skill row for `face_to_size`. That is a process-file change. The generated reference and the MCP guide name the tool.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese open PRs touch the same files, but in other functions (module lists and match arms). The PR that merges second refreshes.\n- #4463, #4238: `crates/ui/src/state.rs`, `crates/app/src/mcp/mod.rs`\n- #4463: `crates/app/src/commands/mod.rs`\n- #4438: `crates/app/src/mcp/mod.rs`\n- #4302, #4288, #4238: `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`\n- #4379, #4288, #4238, #4173: `crates/ui/src/egui_app/mod.rs`\n\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3196#issuecomment-7229330361\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Face to size: one undoable step (Stock page group and MCP tool `face_to_size`) sets a box stock and adds a Face that cuts from a top Z down to a final Z in passes of a stated depth.\n\nFixes #3196\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
